Z||000001||WisconsinGT||10-08-2000||08:13 PM||||I am sure it was recorded well. The problem with the audio is due to the compression used on the clip to make it web compatible. As I mentioned in the original post about the T.V. show, anyone compressing video files for the web should use Sorenson compression. Three benifits that come to mind are...Bigger dimensions, (320x240) smaller file size, (I think the file in question was around 23megs. Using Sorenson you can cut that size in half.) and finally, better audio. (you can have 16 bit stereo audio with minimal loss in sound quality.) FWIW||||reg||1
